{"language_code":"eng","language_probability":0.9919463992118835,"text":"Four friends saved the same hundred dollars a month, and forty years later, one had forty-eight thousand, while another had over four hundred thousand. Wait, how did the same hundred bucks do that? The first hid it under his mattress, and at sixty-two, he had forty-eight thousand, not a dollar more. The second used a savings account paying four percent and ended with about one hundred and eighteen thousand. The third waited until thirty-two, then invested in an index fund averaging about ten percent a year for thirty years and ended with about two hundred and twenty-six thousand. The fourth started that same index fund at twenty-two, and after ten years, he quit. He put in just twelve thousand dollars, and at sixty-two, he had about four hundred and six thousand, more than anyone. His money had ten extra years, and his gains kept earning their own gains, which is called compounding. Same hundred dollars, and the only thing he had more of was time. So which friend are you?","words":[{"text":"Four","start":0.12,"end":0.26,"type":"word","logprob":-0.000025152843591058627},{"text":" ","start":0.26,"end":0.36,"type":"spacing","logprob":-0.000010132738680113107},{"text":"friends","start":0.36,"end":0.6,"type":"word","logprob":-0.000010132738680113107},{"text":" ","start":0.6,"end":0.64,"type":"spacing","logprob":-0.6326044201850891},{"text":"saved","start":0.64,"end":0.8,"type":"word","logprob":-0.6326044201850891},{"text":" ","start":0.8,"end":0.84,"type":"spacing","logprob":-1.1920928244535389e-7},{"text":"the","start":0.84,"end":0.96,"type":"word","logprob":-1.1920928244535389e-7},{"text":" ","start":0.96,"end":1.04,"type":"spacing","logprob":-1.311301275563892e-6},{"text":"same","start":1.04,"end":1.24,"type":"word","logprob":-1.311301275563892e-6},{"text":" ","start":1.24,"end":1.28,"type":"spacing","logprob":-0.0008238735608756542},{"text":"hundred","start":1.28,"end":1.46,"type":"word","logpro